# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repository, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) produces CRLF working
# files, while Prettier's default `endOfLine: "lf"` expects LF — so
# `npm run format:check` (part of `npm run check`) failed locally on nearly
# every file while passing in CI on Linux. Same gate, two different answers
# depending on who runs it.
* text=auto eol=lf
